!.yarn/versions

# Vite logs files
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# Code-structure visualization artifacts (Makefile `viz*` targets)
viz/

# Per-module coverage artifacts (Makefile `cover` / `cover-html` targets)
coverage/
**/coverage.out
**/coverage.html

# The daily fuzz run's findings, log and report (`make fuzz-daily`)
fuzz-out/

# calc module build output
calc/bin/

# Local-run binary from `go run .` / `go build .` inside cmd/go/boru/
cmd/go/boru/boru

# Build artifact occasionally produced under cmd/go (ar archive)
cmd/go/borubin

# Claude Code local worktree / session storage
.claude/

# Test artifacts written by the boru:io IO.write corpus rows
# (lang/spec/corpus-modules.tsv §IO) into the langspec test working
# directory on every `make test` run. Deterministic, not source.
/test/go/langspec/a
/test/go/langspec/c
/test/go/langspec/d
/test/go/langspec/f

# Generated wasm web playground. Built by wpg/Makefile (into ../docs) and
# deployed to GitHub Pages by .github/workflows/pages.yml — the live site
# is rebuilt from the workflow artifact on every push to main, never from
# the repo copy. Committing it only bloated the repo and went stale.
/docs/index.html
/docs/boru.wasm
/docs/wasm_exec.js
/docs/sql-wasm.js
/docs/sql-wasm.wasm

# The generated project knowledge graph bundle is committed on purpose
# (kg/README.md — refresh it with each PR); un-ignore it from the
# Next.js `out` rule above.
!kg/out/

# Python bytecode caches (editors/pygments)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# piecetool builds to coverage/ via `make facades`; never commit the binary.
# Match the binary by PATH, never as a bare name: a bare `piecetool` pattern
# matches the tools/piecetool DIRECTORY too, so every new source file added
# there is silently ignored (tracked files are exempt, which is why that
# stayed invisible). coverage/ is already ignored above, so the make-facades
# build needs no entry of its own.
tools/piecetool/piecetool

# solardemo is a test HTTP fixture built from its own source next to it
# (test/solardemo/{main.go,Makefile,go.mod}); the 8.6MB binary was tracked
# for a long time before this. Build it, don't commit it.
test/solardemo/solardemo

# Scratch probe files. Agent/manual investigation of a parser or dependency
# behaviour writes throwaway probes next to the code it is measuring (the TS
# ones must live inside the package for imports to resolve). They are never
# committed: a stray probe breaks `dupl`, the TS source manifest, and the
# coverage gates. NOTE the modules' own `zz_*_test.go` files (check/go,
# compiler/go) are REAL tests and deliberately not matched here.
**/zz*probe*
zz-*
**/zz_tmp_*
probe.tmp.*
tmpprobe/
